Date: 1/5/20
ORDINANCENO.
ENTITLED:“AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTER 5.52, MASSAGE
ESTABLISHMENTS, WITHIN TITLE 5, BUSINESS LICENSES AND
REGULATIONS, OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE OF THE CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING."
BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING:
Section1.Thatthe following sections of Chapter5.52, Massage Establishments, of Title
5, Business Licenses and Regulations, are hereby amended as set out in this ordinance. Sections
5.52.090
Massage establishment operating requirements.
No person will engage in, conduct or carry on, or permit others to engage in, conduct or carry
on, the operation of a massage business establishment unlesseach of the following requirements are
met:
issued pursuant to the provisions ofthis chapter.It is unlawful forany owner, operator, responsible
managing employee, manager, permittee or licensee in charge of or in control of a massage
establishment to employ or permit any person to act or provide services as a massage therapist who
isnot in possession of avalid permit.
B. The possession of a valid massage establishment license does not authorize the
C.Massage operations shall be carried on, and the premises shall be open, only between
the hours of six a.m.and nine p.m.
D.A list of services available and the cost of such services must be posted in an open
and conspicuous public place on the premises. The service must be described in readily
understandable language.Noowner, operator, responsible managing employee, manager, permitte
or licensee in charge of or in control of the massage business establishment will permit and no
massage therapist will offer to perform nor will they perform, any service other than those posted.
E.  The massage business establishment license, latest public health inspection form and
a copy of the permit of each and every massage therapist employed by or working in the
establishment must be displayed in an open and conspicuous public place on the premises.
