```text
F.A minimum of one toilet and wash basin must be provided for patrons in every
massage establishment; however, if male and female patrons are to be served simultaneously,
separate toilet facilities must be provided for male and female patrons. Hot and cold running water
under pressure must be provided to all wash basins.Each wash basin will be provided with soap or
provided in each toilet room.
G. Clean and sanitary towels, sheets and linens will be provided for each patron
receiving massage services.No common use of towels or linens will be permitted and reuse is
prohibited unless they have been first laundered. Heavy white paper may be substituted for sheets;
provided, that such paperis used once for each person, then discarded into a sanitary receptacle.
H.Disinfecting agents and sanitizing equipment sufficient to assure cleanliness and safe
conditions must be used for any instruments used in performing any massage.
1.Pads used on massage tables must be covered ina workmanlike manner with durable,
washable plastic or other waterproof materials.
 J. Each establishment must provide to all patrons clean, sanitary and opaque coverings
capable ofcovering thepatron's specified anatomical areas.Coverings will be used forone customer
onlyandwill not be reused without first being cleaned.
K.No owner, operator, responsible managing employee, manager, permittee or licensee
in charge of or in control of a massage establishment will permit a massage to be given unless the
patron's specified anatomical areas are covered during the entire massage by the covering referred
to in subsection J of this section except as provided in Section 5.52.105 of this chapter.
L.With the exception of bathrooms or dressing rooms not open to public view, no
owner, operator, responsible managing employee, manager, permit tee or licensee in charge of rn
controlof any massage establishment will permit anypersonin any area ofthe establishment which
is used in common by patrons or which can be viewed by patrons from such an area, unless such
person'sspecified anatomical areas are fully covered.
M.No owner, operator, responsible managing employee, manager, permittee or licensee
in charge of orin control of a massage business establishment will permit any massage therapist to
perform any service or task while inthe presence of a patron or tobe on the premises of a massage
business establishment during its hours of operation unless the massage therapist is fully covered
from a point not to exceed four inches above the center of the kneecap to the base of the neck.Such
covering must be of an opaque material and maintained in a clean and sanitary condition.
2
